# User guides

Write for a person using Alien AI. Short sentences. Everyday words. No system names (identity, webhook, RPC, inst, iid).

Mirrored for Antigravity: [`.agents/rules/docs-guides.md`](../../.agents/rules/docs-guides.md).

## Marketing headline (Indonesian)

Encouraging and simple. Example for create-bot UI:

**Cara membuat chat bot di bawah 5 menit**

Do not add awkward lines like "same result either way." Lead with the outcome and time.

## Outline samples

Before publishing `en/` / `id/` articles, keep working outlines in [`_/docs/samples/`](../../_/docs/samples/README.md). Copy verified steps from the app; note `path: ui` or `path: prompt` at the top.

## Files

English is the source. Indonesian is the same steps, rewritten. Same file name under each language. Screenshots live in that language folder.

```text
_/docs/en/bots/create.md
_/docs/id/bots/create.md
```

## Page

- Headline: what you end up with (or marketing line above for ID landing copy).
- One line: when you would do this.
- Tag: `prompt`, `ui`, or `both`.
- 3 to 5 steps when possible; wizard guides may use numbered substeps.
- Each step says what to do, then what you should see.

Indonesian uses **Anda**.

## Indonesian words that stay English

Use the word people already say. Leave these out: Tautan, Unduh, Unggah. Same for other textbook stand-ins (Sunting, Pranala, Berkas).

| Use | Leave out |
|---|---|
| Link | Tautan |
| Download | Unduh |
| Upload | Unggah |

The home page Docs button lists guides in the site theme. English on `/`, Indonesian on `/id/`.
